## Comparing Core AI Approaches

| Category | Primary Objective | Common Methods / Concepts | Typical Use Cases |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Traditional / Discriminative ML** | Analyze existing data to classify, predict numerical values, or detect anomalies. | Decision trees, regression, support vector machines, classical neural networks. | Credit scoring, spam detection, medical diagnostics, weather forecasting. |
| **Generative AI** | Create new, original content that mirrors the structure of training examples. | Transformers, diffusion models, generative adversarial networks (GANs). | Draft writing, digital art generation, synthetic voice, automated coding. |
| **Large Language Models (LLMs)** | Interpret, generate, and manipulate natural language at scale. | Self-attention mechanisms, token prediction, pre-training, fine-tuning. | Conversational assistants, document summarization, language translation. |
| **Reinforcement Learning (RL)** | Learn optimal decision-making strategies through simulated trial and error. | Agents, environments, reward functions, policies, Q-learning, RLHF. | Robotics navigation, autonomous gameplay, resource allocation, model alignment. |

